Generate today's Higher Ed Intelligence Brief as JSON. Search for 8-10 important stories and output this exact JSON structure:

{"edition": "Month Day, Year", "stats": [{"number": "~4%", "label": "Avg Ivy Accept Rate<br>Class of 2030"}], "keyDates": [{"date": "May 1", "text": "description", "urgent": true}], "todayStories": [{"id": 1, "category": "FEDERAL|LEGAL|ADMISSIONS|INTL|FINANCE|SCHOOL", "urgency": "BREAKING|HIGH|WATCH|INFO", "date": "Mon DD, YYYY", "dayLabel": "Weekday, Month Day", "headline": "text", "summary": "text", "source": "Publication Name", "sourceUrl": "exact URL from search", "schools": ["SchoolName"], "sectorWide": false, "ivyRelevance": "why this matters", "compIntel": "competitive intelligence or null"}], "archiveStories": [same format, stories from past 7 days], "charts": [{"title": "Chart Title", "type": "horizontal_bar|vertical_bar", "sourceText": "Source Name, Date", "sourceUrl": "exact URL", "linkText": "Read full article", "footnote": "optional note", "data": [{"label": "Item", "value": 4.23, "display": "4.23%", "highlight": false, "color": "#2D7D9A"}]}]}

Provide 4 stats, 5-8 key dates, 8-10 today stories, 4-6 archive stories, and 2-4 charts. Use highlight:true for Brown-specific data points. Only chart data explicitly stated in a single source article. Only use approved news sources.
